      "summary": "Peter St. Onge argues that Democrats took both houses of Congress on November 3 because voters were furious about grocery and gas prices and the Iran war, not because they gave the party a mandate. He says the winners are treating the result as one, and are pushing a public health-insurance option, a reparations commission covering more than slavery, and a 5 percent annual wealth tax on billionaires. Citing a Forbes growth figure, he says billionaire capital grows about 5 percent a year, so that tax would take the whole gain, and that the base would later be pulled down toward homeowners and profitable small businesses. He argues a $25 minimum wage would make jobs that produce less than that illegal, and that with a May 2025 median wage of $24.51 an hour this would cover about half of American jobs, about 72 million, hitting teenagers and new workers while AI is already replacing entry-level work. He also says Khanna wants ICE abolished, that Democratic leaders back mass amnesty, and that the incoming House is preparing investigations of Trump donors, RFK Jr., and a long target list that includes Stephen Miller and Trump's children."
